  "notes": [
    "`Velocity_Up`, `Velocity_DR` and `Velocity_CR` read in feet per second, from the manual and the summary: over the climb to the barometer's highest sample, `Velocity_Up` integrates to 1 ft against the barometer's rise of 1 ft, a ratio of 1.00",
    "`Inertial_Altitude`, `Inertial_DR_Position` and `Inertial_CR_position` read in feet, from the manual and the summary: `Inertial_Altitude` peaks at 1 ft against the barometric altitude's 1 ft",
    "13 columns named `Reserved…` hold what the manual doesn't describe, and were kept as written",
    "the logger's time of day, \"Time\", goes back 1 times, by up to 86399.980 s: it is kept as written, and `Flight_Time_(s)` is the clock"
  ]
}
